    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Reviewer 1",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Comment 1.1 — The Ti³⁺ component could be an artefact of differential charging. Please justify.",
          "marks": [
            "bold"
          ],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "We agree this must be excluded. We repeated the measurements with the flood gun at three emission currents; the Ti⁴⁺–Ti³⁺ separation varied by < 0.03 eV (new Table S2). In addition, the Ti³⁺ fraction is reversible upon re-oxidation in 10⁻⁶ mbar O₂, which charging artefacts would not be.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Added (p. 6, l. 142): “The chemical shift was invariant to neutraliser settings within 0.03 eV (Table S2).”",
          "marks": [
            "italic"
          ],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Comment 1.2 — Why is the Lorentzian fraction fixed at 0.3?",
          "marks": [
            "bold"
          ],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Leaving ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "\\eta",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " free led to strong correlation with the FWHM (",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "|\\rho| = 0.94",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": "). We now report a sensitivity analysis over ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "\\eta \\in [0.2, 0.4]",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": "; the Ti³⁺ fraction changes by at most 0.6 %.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Reviewer 2",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Comment 2.1 — The activation energy seems low. Compare with the literature.",
          "marks": [
            "bold"
          ],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "We have added a comparison with three previous studies (new Table 3) and discussed the role of the UHV chemical potential of oxygen, ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "\\Delta\\mu_O(T,p)",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ", which lowers the effective formation energy.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Comment 2.2 — Minor: typo in Eq. (3).",
          "marks": [
            "bold"
          ],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
